{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-13T05:59:08.574Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6cac702086723f6d9ab0b467","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1716"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1716: pm files and pm docs --add silently replace an existing link's note, and the receipt reports it as a plain change"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1716 (filed 2026-11-12). pm files id --add path=P,note=N2 on a path already linked with a different note silently replaces the earlier note, and pm docs --add does the same. The output reports changed true and mutation_receipt changed_count 1, which also describes adding a new link, so an agent cannot tell that it overwrote another agent's rationale; the first note survives only in history, which pm get does not show. Found during a multi-agent review round, where an orchestrator lost the implementer's notes on two paths and had to revert the writes and use a comment instead. Proposal from the issue: refuse an --add whose path and scope already exist with a different non-empty note with a conflict code (for example link_note_conflict) naming the existing note and offering --replace-note (today's behaviour) or --append-note (joins the notes); keep an identical or note-less repeat an idempotent no-op reporting changed false; and make the receipt distinguish added, note_replaced and unchanged per link, for files and docs and the SDK link operations alike."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","docs","files","gh:1716","multi-agent"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-13T05:59:08.574Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-13T05:59:08.574Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"An --add whose path and scope are linked with a different non-empty note is refused with a link conflict code that names the existing note and keeps it; --append-note joins the notes and --replace-note keeps today's behaviour, each recorded in history as one operation; Repeating an identical --add reports changed false, and receipts distinguish added, note_replaced and unchanged per link for files, docs and the SDK"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A note replacement is refused or explicit"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The earlier note is replaced silently and the receipt says changed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-dj98","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-13T05:59:08.574Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"131e73c693960ea1be812e5aa06f37a3078ee05a22fff1ed822d7cfa285efc4f","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_versio