{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-13T15:48:38.311Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1f65549d969a385dd658b1e6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1706","claim:pm-gh1716","claim:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1706+pm-gh1716+pm-jndg9a","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1706","claim:pm-gh1716","claim:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.323","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-13T15:48:38.311Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-13T15:48:38.311Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Progress (branch fix/mutation-outcome-honesty): reproduced on the 2026.11.13 build; mergeLinkedArtifactChanges replaced the note of any existing path+scope match whenever the add carried one. Design: one closed-domain flag --note-conflict refuse|replace|append (default refuse; SDK noteConflict, MCP noteConflict) instead of the issue's two booleans, so no mutual-exclusion rule is needed and the files and docs grammar grows by one flag. The refusal is linked_artifact_note_conflict (exit 4), thrown under the item lock before any write; details.conflicts lists path, scope, existing_note and requested_note; next steps replay the whole invocation with --note-conflict append or replace, carrying the revision guards it ran under and withholding the retry when they cannot be spelled. append joins with '; ' and is idempotent when the text is already a segment. mutation_receipt.link_outcomes reports added, note_added, note_replaced, note_appended or unchanged per requested link; a link first added in the same write takes a later note. Fleet census 2026-11-13: pm-web links files without notes and pm-changelog only reads linked paths, so no released caller re-adds a note. pm update --file keeps the first stored entry and never replaces its note, so it cannot lose rationale."}]}],"before_hash":"7ba353652e72176a33b21fb961f9fccbd078078c51634dc236693f560befe0ca","after_hash":"f4b98c5b87bc55b600e7b976dce4c38e382202fcedf59cb0785a2ed98c2ac916","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"9200fbf87773a8af512c9ecf13ab543519b9c114a316eeee55dda723410d169e"}
