{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-13T16:43:23.876Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1f65549d969a385dd658b1e6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.323","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-13T16:43:23.876Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/contract_change","value":{"api":"pm files and pm docs --add (CLI, SDK runFiles/runDocs, MCP files/docs)","before":"An add on a link already stored with a different note replaced that note and reported a plain change","after":"Such an add is refused with linked_artifact_note_conflict (exit 4) and keeps the stored note; --note-conflict replace overwrites it, --note-conflict append joins the notes, and mutation_receipt.link_outcomes reports what each requested link became","migrate":"Pass --note-conflict replace (SDK and MCP noteConflict) where a re-add is meant to revise the note, or append to keep both; identical and note-less repeats need no change"}}],"before_hash":"d408b97c6305443b8ce47a7cb17f5cc36cb83fb26a515ec359588d2a75f34318","after_hash":"e29457723747919065b0c8192038f1251559dd10cfcb459a1b63884663b0df5a","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Declare the note-conflict contract change","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e6bca2e1f1df60902bceb0d4a22d36bc72ae9545fb5e40f302c879252b41aa22"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-13T17:10:58.592Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1f65549d969a385dd658b1e6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.323","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-13T17:10:58.592Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 1 (Codex gpt-6.1-sol xhigh, Greptile): (1) appending a note that itself contains the joiner was not idempotent; the check now looks for the whole requested text as a run of joined segments. (2) link_outcomes described merge steps, so a batch that revised a note and restored it reported note_replaced although nothing was saved; outcomes are now one per link, judged from the pre-write and final notes. (3) outcome paths now use storage's form (backslashes become slashes), so a migration destination spelled with backslashes reports the saved path. (4) a stdin-resolved literal '-' add, glob or remove entry is replayed in keyed form (path=- or pattern=-) so the retry never reads stdin."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-13T17:10:58.592Z"}],"before_hash":"e29457723747919065b0c8192038f1251559dd10cfcb459a1b63884663b0df5a","after_hash":"f9546d408d9f619dc53d8164e0d078bd11811f3cdf7de95ccdbabb6d3d669a19","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a4711a2f7932e25b9ef67ea26d7e94220f41deb72ea8c6fe7f7ccd8a0d7bfc40"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-13T18:02:28.001Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1f65549d969a385dd658b1e6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.323","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-13T18:02:28.001Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 2 (Codex, CodeRabbit): (1) merge identity used raw paths, so a migration destination spelled with backslashes bypassed the refusal and saved a duplicate; migrated adds, stored links, removes and the add/remove ambiguity check now compare storage's path form. (2) a write naming a new link twice under append was not idempotent, because a same-write entry took the later note while the replay appended; entries of one write now apply in order under one rule, so append and replace replays save nothing and refuse rejects a write whose own notes disagree (details.conflicts[].source this_write, with its own message). (3) the conflict retry names the canonical item id, so a shorthand such as discover never replays as a subcommand."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-13T18:02:28.001Z"}],"before_hash":"f9546d408d9f619dc53d8164e0d078bd11811f3cdf7de95ccdbabb6d3d669a19","after_hash":"c22c975171ec069c555d25980ddc91880ef9fa741d53ba4bea5a5dabe49de527","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f40b6bcdff8b8dbb9e63790f8b3e0b12d3d7c2d42dec5e247cd633e2c7c4c924"}
